    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B08",
      "act": "THE SCAM PARALLEL",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "tone": "sober, no outrage — say it plainly and let it sit",
      "narration_text": "And here's why this matters. Back in April 2025, Tunefind put out a warning. People were emailing artists, pretending to be Tunefind, promising placements for money. And the thing that made those emails convincing? Real shows. Real placements. True facts, doing the work of a lie.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "REMOTION",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "WantQuote916",
          "props": {
            "quote": "…may even include fake licensing agreements or references to real shows.",
            "attribution": "Tunefind, 8 April 2025",
            "sparkLine": "The scammers found this first.",
            "dataNote": ""
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B08.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B08.mp3",
      "estimated_duration_s": 15.0,
      "actual_duration_s": 19.54,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B08.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-08-24T00:06:37"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B09",
      "act": "YOUR TURN",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice": "af_bella",
      "tone": "practical and generous — handing something over",
      "narration_text": "So before you send anything, go down the layers. First: did this person actually work on this show? Second: is the song really in it? Third: is the detail right? And then the one nobody asks — whose decision was it? And on those song sites, read the little label. Music Supervisor Verified means they confirmed it themselves. Questions means somebody is arguing about it.",
